{"parentUuid":"bcf3808e-b741-477a-bc43-0d47ca75db0c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JsdsYEBKVnMN56BeFaFgbF","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools Release Management Discussion Summary\n\nBased on the GitHub discussion, here's what was disclosed about OR-Tools release practices:\n\n## Release Strategy\n\nThe maintainers explained their branching approach. The `main` branch serves as the development branch, closely synchronized with Google's internal codebase. The `stable` branch always points to the latest release tag and is the default branch users receive.\n\n## Upcoming Releases\n\nAccording to the discussion, \"the current plan is to do a 9.13 soon without a release candidate (next week, or the week after, no promise). Then quickly do a 10.0 rc1 which will break compatibility with the routing library.\"\n\nA `v99bugfix` branch exists for testing pre-release versions. The maintainers stated: \"So v99bugfix branch is pretty close to release. Please hammer away at it :-)\"\n\n## Release Cadence\n\nThe discussion doesn't specify exact timing between releases, but indicates the team aims for relatively frequent updates. Version 9.13 was expected imminently when this discussion occurred (March 2025).\n\n**Note:** The discussion doesn't mention versions 9.16 or changes since 9.15, as it predates those releases. No specific release management changes were announced."}]},"uuid":"a3e07ee6-42f1-46f3-9925-414065a15080","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:00.095Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bcf3808e-b741-477a-bc43-0d47ca75db0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fb1666e2-8203-4d17-99ae-88d47a4d8c22","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111d8KfJTnPaShDKqS9cFqe","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Performance Issue Summary\n\n## Issue Overview\nA user reported concerns about CP-SAT solver reliability when testing different core configurations using OR-Tools version 9.14.6206 in Python.\n\n## Identified Bottlenecks\nThe main performance challenges mentioned are:\n\n1. **Randomness/Non-determinism**: \"the CP_SAT's randomness makes the results unreliable\" when evaluating performance across different configurations\n\n2. **Interleave Search Overhead**: Enabling `interleave_search=True` causes \"a significant increase in runtime\"\n\n## Resolution/Suggestions\nThe issue was submitted as a question rather than with a proposed solution. The user asked: \"is there a way to obtain deterministic results without causing such a substantial increase in runtime?\"\n\nThe issue remains open in the v9.15 milestone, assigned to maintainer lperron.\n\n## New Parameters\nOnly one parameter is explicitly mentioned: `interleave_search` (a boolean setting for search strategy)\n\n## Packing Problem Guidance\nNo specific recommendations for 2D packing or placement problems are provided in this issue content."}]},"uuid":"8e170591-8bd8-49fe-b117-7ab118b9d326","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:01.580Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb1666e2-8203-4d17-99ae-88d47a4d8c22","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c0b55b1d-2229-43b5-8ff2-d194aebf6726","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XdrJ1gHCHBNyLWhq4vXyPQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the web page content provided, there is only **one closed CP-SAT issue** listed for the v9.16 milestone:\n\n**#4985** - \"solver.status_name() raises TypeError: 'ortools.sat.python.cp_model_helper.CpSolverStatus' object is not callable\"\n\n**Summary:** A bug in the Python wrapper where calling `solver.status_name()` throws a TypeError because the object is not callable. The issue was reported by gacheiro and closed on February 26, 2026.\n\nThe page shows search results filtered for closed issues with the \"Solver: CP-SAT Solver\" label in the v9.16 milestone, but only this single issue is displayed in the results section provided."}]},"uuid":"580f5af9-f664-4dc6-b256-8f2e4e1de1fb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:02.913Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0b55b1d-2229-43b5-8ff2-d194aebf6726","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
