{"parentUuid":"b08bda9e-5b79-43a2-a88d-c033a897ac4f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Te2YU1MyC79zyGppmFF3tr","type":"tool_result","content":"# Commit Analysis: CP-SAT Scheduling Cuts and Issue #4875\n\nBased on the GitHub commit page provided, I can identify that this commit modified 67 files with 4,603 additions and 2,391 deletions across the OR-Tools repository's SAT solver module.\n\n## Scheduling Cut Optimizations\n\nThe commit includes changes to `scheduling_cuts.cc` and `scheduling_cuts.h`, indicating algorithmic improvements to how scheduling constraints are generated. However, **the specific optimization details are not visible** in the provided webpage content, which only shows file names and line counts rather than the actual code changes.\n\n## Issue #4875\n\nThe commit message references \"fix #4875\" but **the actual issue description is not included** in the webpage content provided. The page shows only the commit metadata and file structure, not linked issue details.\n\n## What We Can Confirm\n\nThe changes include:\n- New files: `integer_resolution.cc/h` and `lrat_proof_handler.cc/h`\n- Updates to constraint handling and proof generation systems\n- Build system modifications (BUILD.bazel) to wire new components\n\nTo learn the specific scheduling optimizations and Issue #4875's details, you would need to visit the actual issue tracker or view the complete diff content on GitHub."}]},"uuid":"aa0dcabd-b905-4ed1-a0bd-32068da13c4c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:30.426Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b08bda9e-5b79-43a2-a88d-c033a897ac4f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"113ed664-6205-4a0c-9260-b2807b25d6da","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNQ7BJ2UpETNGTKcj28zdi","type":"tool_result","content":"# Issue #4875 Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Interleave search option ignores assumptions\"\n\n**Nature:** This is a bug in the CP-SAT solver's Python wrapper affecting assumption handling when interleave search is enabled.\n\n**Description:** When solving a constraint satisfaction model with the `interleave_search=True` option, the solver incorrectly ignores the assumptions parameter. The reported example shows a model that should be unsatisfiable under given assumptions, yet returns feasible instead.\n\n**Expected vs. Actual Behavior:** With assumptions applied, the solver should return `UNSATISFIABLE` with unset variable values. Instead, it returns `FEASIBLE` and assigns values, demonstrating the assumptions were disregarded.\n\n**Affected Versions:** The issue affects CPMpy v9.14.6206 and was filed in October 2025, targeting the v10.0 Beta milestone. Users on 9.15 would likely experience the same problem.\n\n**Problem Type:** This is neither a scheduling nor no_overlap bug—it's a core assumption-handling defect in the interleave search functionality."}]},"uuid":"590fc656-5989-4127-ba4c-0d797c35999a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:31.426Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"113ed664-6205-4a0c-9260-b2807b25d6da","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"db8a5f7a-43ec-4e29-b44a-40d9a01d6690","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lc3uTNdcTb7xozW69oaVy7","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Commit b5105a6 Analysis\n\n## Scheduling Bug Fixes\n\nThe commit message indicates fixes for **\"wrong explanations; unsafe heuristics\"** in scheduling, though specific details aren't fully visible in the diff provided. The changes affect scheduling-related files including `scheduling_helpers.cc`, `disjunctive.cc`, `intervals.cc`, and `timetable_edgefinding.cc`.\n\n## Key Changes by Category\n\n### Rectangle/2D Scheduling\n- **2d_rectangle_presolve.cc**: Added size check before greedy box reduction to prevent processing single-box cases\n- **2d_try_edge_propagator.cc**: Modified propagation logic to handle optional values, improving explanation safety\n\n### Proof & Clause Management\n- **clause.cc/clause.h**: Enhanced LRAT proof handling with new `RemoveFixedImplications()` method and proof parameter support in `InprocessingAddClause()`\n- **lrat_proof_handler**: Extended to track binary clauses with metadata on implication graph membership\n\n### API Improvements\nMultiple constraint classes now support method chaining:\n- `CircuitConstraint::AddArc()` returns reference\n- `TableConstraint::AddTuple()` returns reference  \n- `ReservoirConstraint::AddEvent()` and `AddOptionalEvent()` return references\n- `NoOverlapConstraint`, `NoOverlap2DConstraint`, `CumulativeConstraint`, `AutomatonConstraint` updated similarly\n\n## sat_parameters.proto Changes\n\nThe diff shown doesn't reveal specific new parameters added to `sat_parameters.proto` (file appears modified but changes aren't detailed in visible content).\n\n## New Additions\n\nA new **debug_solution** library was added to BUILD.bazel for solution validation purposes."}]},"uuid":"696baca0-27b6-4519-85ce-3f976f0b5b72","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:32.065Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db8a5f7a-43ec-4e29-b44a-40d9a01d6690","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7e57b2b5-5d44-4c30-a349-637247bcdb4c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZw77s2WeFcxzcpZkSvd9T","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Parameters Search Results\n\n## Parameters Containing \"no_overlap\", \"scheduling\", \"diffn\", \"packing\", \"cumulative\"\n\nBased on the file content, here are relevant parameters:\n\n**no_overlap/scheduling related:**\n- `use_precedences_in_disjunctive_constraint` (Tag 74, bool, default=true)\n- `max_size_to_create_precedence_literals_in_disjunctive` (Tag 229, int32, default=60)\n- `use_strong_propagation_in_disjunctive` (Tag 230, bool, default=false)\n- `use_dynamic_precedence_in_disjunctive` (Tag 263, bool, default=false)\n- `transitive_precedences_work_limit` (Tag 327, int32, default=1000000)\n\n**cumulative related:**\n- `use_overload_checker_in_cumulative` (Tag 78, bool, default=false)\n- `use_dynamic_precedence_in_cumulative` (Tag 268, bool, default=false)\n\n**Note:** No parameters explicitly containing \"diffn\" or \"packing\" appear in the visible portion.\n\n## Parameters Containing \"feasibility_jump\", \"violation_ls\", \"shaving\", \"probing\"\n\n**probing related (visible in file):**\n- `probing_deterministic_time_limit` (Tag 226, double, default=1.0)\n- `presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit` (Tag 57, double, default=30.0)\n- `cp_model_probing_level` (Tag 110, int32, default=2)\n- `inprocessing_probing_dtime` (Tag 274, double, default=1.0)\n\n**Note:** \"feasibility_jump\", \"violation_ls\", and \"shaving\" do not appear in the provided content.\n\n## Highest Tag Number\n\nThe highest visible tag in the file is **362** (mentioned in the header comment \"NEXT TAG: 362\")."}]},"uuid":"ab5f9388-8746-49db-b2da-f5aa87cf82ea","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:33.438Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7e57b2b5-5d44-4c30-a349-637247bcdb4c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cl