{"parentUuid":"66c1521e-7b21-4567-b670-c7bffe554a45","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KpE1kzjcCxD8sW9g3fsqdp","type":"tool_result","content":"# Issue #4988 Summary\n\n**Title:** CpSolver.Solve() callback breaking argument change\n\n**What it's about:** \nThe deprecated `CpSolver.Solve()` method inadvertently became incompatible with existing code. When the API was refactored to favor the lowercase `.solve()` method, the parameter name was accidentally changed from `solution_callback` to `callback`, breaking backward compatibility.\n\n**Severity:** \nHigh for affected users—code using the old API with the correct parameter name now throws a TypeError instead of receiving a deprecation warning.\n\n**Affects version 9.15?**\nYes. The issue was opened on January 15, 2026, and targets version 9.15.6755 in the Python API.\n\n**Workaround:**\nSwitch to the lowercase `.solve()` method, which still accepts the `solution_callback` parameter correctly:\n```python\nsolver.solve(model, solution_callback=MyCallback())\n```\n\n**Status:**\nThe issue is marked as Open and assigned to the milestone v9.16, suggesting a fix is planned but not yet released."}]},"uuid":"329a724d-42c7-4993-be0b-44321bcf1ec5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:43.657Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66c1521e-7b21-4567-b670-c7bffe554a45","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
