{"parentUuid":"8c14563d-749e-41fd-8a4f-af22da45a385","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rjPmgM9n93JkBdgs1tELK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Commits to 2d_rectangle_presolve.cc Since September 2025\n\nBased on the GitHub history provided, here are the relevant commits:\n\n| SHA | Date | Title | Algorithmic Notes |\n|-----|------|-------|-------------------|\n| c6772d4 | Feb 23, 2026 | \"base: rework logging management\" | Infrastructure change, not algorithmic |\n| b5105a6 | Feb 19, 2026 | \"[CP-SAT] fix scheduling bugs: wrong explanations; unsafe heuristics; more work on lrat; switch max_hs to use CP-SAT as MIP solver; other bugfixes\" | Bug fixes in scheduling and heuristics |\n| 694a9b0 | Jan 20, 2026 | \"Split graph folder (#4998)\" | Code organization, not algorithmic |\n| 11f02a5 | Dec 24, 2025 | \"Fix warning 'control reaches end of non-void function'\" | Compiler warning fix |\n| e02b6a0 | Aug 22, 2025 | \"[CP-SAT] update code, mostly small bug fixes\" | Outside the September 2025 cutoff |\n\n**No algorithmic improvements directly targeting 2D placement/packing or no_overlap_2d constraints** appear in commits after September 2025. The relevant work on these topics occurred in earlier commits (December 2024 and prior), including efforts on \"2d packing presolve\" and \"no_overlap_2d cuts.\""}]},"uuid":"7778909e-bab8-4092-a7df-2e9e9f538131","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:48.423Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c14563d-749e-41fd-8a4f-af22da45a385","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ae9f7612-0fcb-436b-816b-7a4610aeba00","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LYNwniTW7opkjqG4PjEj23","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recent CP-SAT LNS Changes (Since October 2025)\n\nBased on the commit history, here are the notable developments:\n\n## New LNS Strategies/Neighborhoods\n\n**Packing LNS** - Introduced in December 2024 commit, a new neighborhood focusing on packing problems. The commit notes: \"new packing LNS; propagate objective in LNS\"\n\n**Graph-based LNS** - Mentioned in March 2025 work: \"graph based LNS start from the objective\"\n\n## Key Improvements\n\nSeveral optimization efforts emerged:\n\n- **Memory optimization** (February 2025): \"improve memory usage for LNS\"\n- **Model reduction strategies** (March 2026): Work on \"LNS and LS model reductions when possible\"\n- **Routing enhancements** (March 2025): \"more work on routing cuts\"\n\n## Solver/Subsolver Work\n\nWhile the commits don't explicitly detail new subsolver additions, there was significant architectural work including \"simplify lns model when possible\" and improvements to time limit enforcement during LNS solving.\n\nThe most recent commits focus on code cleanup and gate improvements rather than introducing entirely new LNS strategies."}]},"uuid":"e527122d-8ad8-413d-ace9-f3e7dfa478c9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:48.868Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae9f7612-0fcb-436b-816b-7a4610aeba00","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
