{"parentUuid":"3a8ea99b-96e3-4eec-8773-c8052921839a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NJWS1TDu8sRs1VCrSLDF9d","type":"tool_result","content":"# New SatParameters Fields (Tags 356-361)\n\n**Tag 356: num_ordering_in_vivification**\n- Type: int32\n- Default: 1\n- Description: \"The number of ordering to try each time we vivify a clause. This allow to spend more effort on vivivication if needed.\"\n\n**Tag 357: detect_encoded_complex_domain**\n- Type: bool\n- Default: true\n- Description: Attempts to identify and remove Boolean variables used solely for encoding domains with holes (like [0][2,5][7][9]), detecting such patterns and removing unnecessary encoding variables.\n\n**Tag 358: mip_scale_to_max_bound**\n- Type: bool\n- Default: false\n- Description: When enabled, scales floating-point variables by powers of two to fit within [-mip_max_bound, mip_max_bound], overriding mip_var_scaling and mip_scale_large_domain settings.\n\n**Tag 359: mip_presolve_restrict_bounds**\n- Type: bool\n- Default: true\n- Description: Applies dual-reasoning to constrain variable domains before converting the model to integers, potentially improving scaling outcomes.\n\n**Tag 360: cp_model_pure_sat_presolve**\n- Type: bool\n- Default: false\n- Description: \"Whether to use a simplified pure sat presolve only when cp_model_presolve is true. Crashes if the model is not pure SAT.\"\n\n**Tag 361: inprocessing_use_transitive_reduction**\n- Type: bool\n- Default: true\n- Description: Performs transitive reduction on the binary implication graph, potentially reducing implications but risking loss of structural information used by detection algorithms."}]},"uuid":"192b55ec-f41f-444a-a0fe-847db79d1fe1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:00.056Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3a8ea99b-96e3-4eec-8773-c8052921839a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\clau