{"parentUuid":"926161d2-7218-4b9d-b4ed-68ba467f5faa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GDa4FvjfQgJCNQ9PLzq2mR","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the webpage content provided, I can only identify **one closed issue** from the v9.16 milestone:\n\n1. **#4985** - \"solver.status_name() raises TypeError: 'ortools.sat.python.cp_model_helper.CpSolverStatus' object is not callable\"\n\nUnfortunately, the page content you've shared only displays this single issue result. To see a comprehensive list of 20-30 closed issues from the v9.16 milestone, you would need to:\n\n- Visit the full GitHub issues page for google/or-tools with the filter applied\n- Scroll through multiple pages of results, or\n- Adjust pagination settings if available\n\nThe current excerpt doesn't contain the breadth of fixes you're looking for—it appears to be just the first issue on a filtered search results page."}]},"uuid":"61815795-dc62-4bba-8ecd-aa4b0a357557","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:00.070Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"926161d2-7218-4b9d-b4ed-68ba467f5faa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3fdafbed-1bff-4f91-8e5f-7636739124ad","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"a656b69d449b928b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013LMmir7jgN4Q7RtRAYSXKj","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP Model Presolve Commits Since September 2025\n\nBased on the commit history, here are the notable updates to `cp_model_presolve.cc`:\n\n**Key Improvements:**\n\n1. **LRAT Proof Work** - Multiple commits focused on implementing and improving LRAT (Logical Redundancy Added Transitivity) proof generation, with enhancements to the proof checker.\n\n2. **Encoding Optimizations** - Substantial work on variable encoding strategies, including \"better expansion of variables only appearing in encoding constraints\" and improvements to linear1 and linear2 encoding methods.\n\n3. **Enforcement Literals** - Extended support allowing \"all constraints now support enforcement literals\" with arbitrary linear expression handling.\n\n4. **Bug Fixes & Tuning** - Regular fixes including scheduling constraint improvements, vivification bug corrections, and safety enhancements in heuristics.\n\n5. **Constraint Merging** - Implementation of no_overlap_2d constraint merging during presolve for improved problem reduction.\n\nThe commits emphasize proof generation capabilities, constraint handling sophistication, and incremental performance tuning rather than introducing entirely new presolve rules."}]},"uuid":"a73f090b-1a58-4497-8025-94d41f6a8ab3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:02.509Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3fdafbed-1bff-4f91-8e5f-7636739124ad","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
